  "body": "## What changed\n\nThe gate keeps successful libtest output with `--show-output`. It reports each named GPU skip in the step summary. A successful process with incomplete GPU coverage has a `SKIP` row, not an `ok` row. Missing adapters use `SKIPPED (no adapter): <test>`. Other GPU refusals remain distinct.\n\nThe adapter report names the device that wgpu returned. It includes the backend and device type. CPU devices report software. Integrated and discrete GPUs report hardware. Virtual and other devices report unknown hardware identity.\n\nThe decision keeps the post-merge policy at \"skip, but report\". This change does not alter workflows, runners, adapter selection, kernels, parity assertions, tolerances or CPU fallback behavior.\n\n## Verification\n\nFinal head: `99858f35ba6a42a7744804a2d9e76984bf2db3df`.\n\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main`: PASS. Both selected steps ran: GPU library tests and xtask unit tests.\n- `cargo test -p xtask gpu_reporting`: PASS. The tests cover captured parallel output, mixed CPU passes and GPU skips, deduplication, adapter identity, unknown identity, and failure reporting.\n- The new reporting tests failed before the fix. The captured-output test also failed without `--show-output`.\n- `cargo xtask gate test the_gpu_cut_onto_a_keyframe_matches_the_cpu_law_or_skips_by_name --crate camcraft-gpu --binary cut_onto --exact`: PASS on software `llvmpipe (LLVM 21.1.8, 256 bits)` via Vulkan, device type Cpu.\n- A process-scoped Vulkan-disabled probe ran the same parity test on hardware `Mesa Intel(R) UHD Graphics 630 (CFL GT2)` via Gl, device type IntegratedGpu. This is evidence for this one small test on this host, not general hardware coverage.\n- With process-scoped `VK_DRIVER_FILES=/nonexistent __EGL_VENDOR_LIBRARY_FILENAMES=/nonexistent DISPLAY= WAYLAND_DISPLAY=`, the same gate printed a named `SKIPPED (no adapter)` and a `SKIP` row. Its exit code was zero under the existing skip policy.\n- Adding `CAMCRAFT_REQUIRE_GPU=1` to that absent-adapter probe produced `FAIL` and exit code 1, as expected.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-gpu --all-targets -- -D warnings`: PASS.\n- Strict xtask clippy fails on the unchanged `clippy::needless_bool` in `xtask/src/unit_sweep.rs:67`. This failure was reproduced before the edits. `cargo clippy -p xtask --all-targets -- -D warnings -A clippy::needless_bool`: PASS. No source lint allowance was added.\n- `git diff --check`: PASS.\n\n## Limits and process\n\nThe light dry-run selects unrelated motion/app release builds and six steps. Those steps were not run for this reporting-only change. No full workspace, release, catalog or GUI build ran. Synthetic fixtures do not establish hardware parity. No maintainer runner or workflow was started. `graphify` is not installed on this host.\n\nThe first quick invocation reached the xtask tests but exceeded a 180-second tool timeout. The later full quick runs completed successfully. This timeout is not presented as a pass.\n\nNo scout was commissioned. Bounded direct discovery inspected `xtask/src/exec.rs`, `direct.rs`, `budget.rs`, `tests.rs`, the GPU adapter and shared harness, and equivalent skip diagnostics. No compute or safety algorithm changed. The existing `gpu_render` local cache emits its diagnostic only at initial device creation; this change reports diagnostics that the harness emits, not inferred skips from tests with no diagnostic.\n\nEffort: medium\n\nProcess change: yes\n\nChangelog: The gate reports named GPU skips and the actual adapter instead of hiding missing coverage behind a successful process exit.\n\nFixes #3879\n",
